1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:04,587
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:04,671 --> 00:00:05,672
<i>Jordan.</i>

3
00:00:08,216 --> 00:00:10,343
[JORDAN] <i>What are you doing here?</i>

4
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:11,970
<i>Did you break out?</i>

5
00:00:12,053 --> 00:00:13,388
<i>Is that what a changed person does?</i>

6
00:00:13,471 --> 00:00:16,099
You even escaped with Caloy Toledo.

7
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:18,143
<i>He became my friend while we were inside.</i>

8
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:20,729
<i>But I didn't know you two were enemies.</i>

9
00:00:20,812 --> 00:00:24,107
<i>I know I've hurt you and your mom.</i>

10
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:26,735
<i>That's why I'm here now.</i>
<i>To make amends.</i>

11
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:28,403
<i>What do I need to do</i>

12
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:32,282
<i>to prove to you that I regret everything?</i>

13
00:00:33,658 --> 00:00:36,453
[JORDAN] <i>Show me where Carlos Toledo is.</i>

14
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:39,414
<i>Caloy!</i>

15
00:00:39,497 --> 00:00:46,463
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

16
00:00:50,508 --> 00:00:54,846
[GRUNTING, BLOWS LANDING]

17
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:56,681
- [GRUNTS]
- [THUD]

18
00:00:57,223 --> 00:01:00,185
- [CALOY]<i> All right!</i>
- [DINO]<i> Give that to me!</i>

19
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:01,770
- [GUNSHOT]
- [DINO GROANS]

20
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:04,355
[DINO GRUNTS, GROANS]

21
00:01:07,025 --> 00:01:09,235
[DOCTOR] <i>She suffered a head trauma.</i>

22
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:12,489
<i>However, we didn't find</i>
<i>any internal bleeding.</i>

23
00:01:12,572 --> 00:01:15,075
<i>But she needs to be under observation</i>

24
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:17,827
<i>for at least another 24 hours.</i>

25
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:20,789
[ENRICO] <i>Thank you, Doc.</i>

26
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:27,837
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

27
00:01:28,922 --> 00:01:31,049
<i>I have to go somewhere.</i>

28
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:32,801
<i>Take care of your father for now, okay?</i>

29
00:01:32,884 --> 00:01:34,844
<i>I'll go ahead.</i>

30
00:01:34,928 --> 00:01:36,095
<i>Thank you, son.</i>

31
00:01:38,389 --> 00:01:39,891
<i>I'll be back, okay? I'll be quick.</i>

32
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:41,017
<i>Wait.</i>

33
00:01:43,561 --> 00:01:45,063
<i>Jade, I…</i>

34
00:01:46,147 --> 00:01:49,651
<i>I got a job from Teban earlier.</i>

35
00:01:50,985 --> 00:01:52,153
<i>Um…</i>

36
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:55,156
<i>I got this for you.</i>

37
00:01:55,240 --> 00:02:01,371
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

38
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:05,750
[JADE SNIFFLES]

39
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:11,756
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

40
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:19,430
<i>This is expensive.</i>

41
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:23,893
<i>It's because I love you so much.</i>

42
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:25,186
<i>I didn't…</i>

43
00:02:26,396 --> 00:02:29,357
<i>I didn't mean to do that.</i>

44
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:31,067
<i>It won't happen again.</i>

45
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:33,444
<i>I promise.</i>

46
00:02:36,322 --> 00:02:37,532
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

47
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:39,617
<i>Sorry.</i>

48
00:02:41,327 --> 00:02:44,789
[SNIFFLES, SOBS]

49
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:48,334
[JADE SOBBING]

50
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:50,378
<i>That necklace belonged to my mom.</i>

51
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:54,757
<i>This is mine. Your father gave it to me.</i>

52
00:02:57,343 --> 00:03:04,350
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

53
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:09,105
[ATTY. GRANADO] <i>Due to your withdrawal,</i>

54
00:03:09,188 --> 00:03:11,566
<i>the Court dismissed Bea's cases</i>
<i>without prejudice</i>

55
00:03:11,649 --> 00:03:13,860
<i>on the grounds</i>
<i>of insufficiency of evidence</i>

56
00:03:13,943 --> 00:03:15,904
<i>and unavailability of witnesses.</i>

57
00:03:15,987 --> 00:03:17,989
But we need to file for medical clearance.

58
00:03:18,072 --> 00:03:19,490
She can come home tomorrow.

59
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:21,451
Okay, Attorney. Thank you.

60
00:03:22,201 --> 00:03:24,245
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

61
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:26,205
- [PHONE THUDS]
- [CHAIR SCRAPES]

62
00:03:27,206 --> 00:03:29,834
- [BILLY GRUNTS SOFTLY]
- Will you visit her, Billy?

63
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:35,173
Dad's there. He can handle it.

64
00:03:35,882 --> 00:03:39,177
What about you? Can you handle it?

65
00:03:40,929 --> 00:03:44,098
Are you sure there's nothing
I can do to help you?

66
00:03:46,976 --> 00:03:48,019
I'm okay.

67
00:03:50,939 --> 00:03:52,774
You know, Billy,

68
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:55,652
people who say that they're okay

69
00:03:55,735 --> 00:03:59,197
are often the ones who need help.

70
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:01,241
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

71
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:02,408
[PRECIOUS] So tell me.

72
00:04:02,492 --> 00:04:04,827
But first, let's eat together.
The food is good.

73
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:06,996
- [BILLY HALF-LAUGHS]
- [PRECIOUS] Come on.

74
00:04:08,039 --> 00:04:09,165
[PRECIOUS] It's so good.

75
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:11,376
Where's Oliver, Auntie?

76
00:04:11,459 --> 00:04:13,002
He's sleeping already.

77
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:18,341
Is something wrong, Billy?

78
00:04:21,678 --> 00:04:25,056
I just don't know how to tell him that

79
00:04:26,015 --> 00:04:28,351
he has another sister.

80
00:04:28,434 --> 00:04:34,482
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

81
00:04:35,984 --> 00:04:41,906
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

82
00:05:40,882 --> 00:05:44,135
- [HEAVY FOOTSTEPS]
- [CAR HONKING IN DISTANCE]

83
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:58,608
My dear.

84
00:05:58,691 --> 00:06:04,947
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:07,700
Pa.

86
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:11,704
Your sister called me.

87
00:06:12,705 --> 00:06:14,749
Attorney Granado said

88
00:06:15,416 --> 00:06:18,127
you can get out
once we get your clearance.

89
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:24,133
You're not going to go back to jail, dear.

90
00:06:25,176 --> 00:06:26,636
[SIGHS SHARPLY]

91
00:06:31,057 --> 00:06:32,475
Thank you.

92
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:40,441
What's that?

93
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:42,693
Oh.

94
00:06:46,572 --> 00:06:47,615
Letters.

95
00:06:47,698 --> 00:06:54,705
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

96
00:06:57,667 --> 00:07:00,711
I wrote those letters
for you and your siblings.

97
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:06,843
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

98
00:07:08,469 --> 00:07:12,223
I expressed there
how much I missed all of you

99
00:07:12,306 --> 00:07:13,891
and how sorry I was.

100
00:07:16,185 --> 00:07:22,066
It's too bad Abi won't be able
to read my letters to her.

101
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:26,279
I wrote those when I was
imprisoned in Canada.

102
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:32,452
I promised myself that
when I got out of jail…

103
00:07:35,079 --> 00:07:38,332
I'd make amends to all of you
for all my shortcomings.

104
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:47,842
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

105
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:54,974
[SNIFFLES]

106
00:07:56,934 --> 00:08:00,104
Even if I read these,

107
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:03,149
nothing would change.

108
00:08:05,193 --> 00:08:07,487
It won't bring back…

109
00:08:10,948 --> 00:08:12,575
what I've lost.

110
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:19,665
[MUSIC BECOMES EMOTIONAL]

111
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:27,548
[BEA SNIFFLES]

112
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:31,761
Like I told your sister…

113
00:08:35,598 --> 00:08:39,852
I don't expect you
to forgive me completely.

114
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:42,563
[ENRICO SNIFFLES]

115
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:43,814
But, my dear,

116
00:08:44,982 --> 00:08:47,401
please don't waste this opportunity…

117
00:08:50,446 --> 00:08:52,365
to start anew.

118
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:55,660
I'm trying to start over too.

119
00:08:57,870 --> 00:08:59,288
With you

120
00:09:00,831 --> 00:09:02,458
and your siblings.

121
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:11,968
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

122
00:09:21,602 --> 00:09:23,604
Pa, I can feel…

123
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:27,358
how sincerely sorry you are.

124
00:09:28,192 --> 00:09:29,944
[BEA INHALES DEEPLY]

125
00:09:30,027 --> 00:09:31,529
So, these don't matter now.

126
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:39,579
What's important is…

127
00:09:42,456 --> 00:09:43,833
you're here now.

128
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:46,210
Yes, dear.

129
00:09:49,171 --> 00:09:50,548
I'm here now.

130
00:10:00,474 --> 00:10:07,398
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

131
00:10:19,869 --> 00:10:21,412
Stop crying now.

132
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:41,557
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

133
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:43,059
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

134
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:57,323
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:10:57,406 --> 00:10:59,075
- [BANGING ON DOOR]
<i>- Open up!</i>

136
00:11:02,036 --> 00:11:03,829
<i>Where's my son? I want to see him.</i>

137
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:05,539
<i>See him or take him?</i>

138
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:09,085
<i>I swore on my daughter's grave</i>
<i>that I would protect Jordan.</i>

139
00:11:09,168 --> 00:11:12,671
<i>I won't let my grandson live</i>
<i>with a father like you.</i>

140
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:14,590
<i>I also called the police.</i>

141
00:11:15,466 --> 00:11:16,759
[SLAMS]

142
00:11:17,468 --> 00:11:19,595
<i>You will regret this, you hear me?!</i>

143
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:31,649
<i>Really? That Jordan is your son? Him?</i>

144
00:11:32,566 --> 00:11:35,653
<i>Don't you see? It says "Jordan Valentin."</i>

145
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:37,154
<i>His surname is Valentin.</i>

146
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:42,660
[JORDAN SINGING IN VIDEO]
<i>♪ Where is our destination? ♪</i>

147
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:46,872
<i>Let's say</i>

148
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:51,544
<i>that he wasn't famous</i>
<i>and hadn't achieved anything in life.</i>

149
00:11:51,627 --> 00:11:53,129
<i>That he didn't own a business.</i>

150
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:55,548
<i>Would you still approach him?</i>

151
00:11:57,508 --> 00:11:59,260
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

152
00:11:59,343 --> 00:12:00,511
<i>Yes.</i>

153
00:12:01,470 --> 00:12:05,641
<i>I have to make amends</i>
<i>for all of my shortcomings.</i>

154
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:14,900
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

155
00:12:45,848 --> 00:12:46,891
Grandpa.

156
00:12:51,687 --> 00:12:53,355
Dad visited me, Gramps.

157
00:12:57,401 --> 00:12:58,903
He apologized.

158
00:13:00,237 --> 00:13:01,864
He said he'll change.

159
00:13:01,947 --> 00:13:08,871
[WISTFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

160
00:13:14,793 --> 00:13:16,086
I remember…

161
00:13:18,589 --> 00:13:21,217
he made that promise
to me and Mom many times.

162
00:13:28,098 --> 00:13:29,600
He would hurt us.

163
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:33,521
Then, he would cry in regret.

164
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:38,359
Then, he'd promise he'd change.

165
00:13:38,442 --> 00:13:43,364
[WISTFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

166
00:13:47,868 --> 00:13:50,246
[JORDAN CLICKS TONGUE, SIGHS DEEPLY]

167
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,499
But he did something this time.

168
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:57,962
For the first time,

169
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:00,714
he protected me.

170
00:14:01,423 --> 00:14:04,385
In fact, he saved my life twice.

171
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:09,765
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

172
00:14:18,649 --> 00:14:21,277
Sir Jordan, visiting hours are over.

173
00:14:22,152 --> 00:14:23,737
I'm here to take the dishes.

174
00:14:23,821 --> 00:14:24,780
Okay.

175
00:14:31,704 --> 00:14:32,872
All right, Grandpa.

176
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:36,500
I'm leaving now.

177
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:37,501
Okay?

178
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:39,461
Good night.

179
00:14:46,093 --> 00:14:52,349
[WISTFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

180
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:54,059
Jade. Dear!

181
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:57,438
Promise me…

182
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:02,234
you won't let your husband fool you again.

183
00:15:03,944 --> 00:15:06,280
For your child's sake!

184
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:11,452
For so long,

185
00:15:12,703 --> 00:15:15,164
you hid from me that he was abusing you.

186
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:19,293
You didn't tell me the truth!

187
00:15:21,503 --> 00:15:23,005
But what did that get you?

188
00:15:25,883 --> 00:15:28,552
You just suffered even more!

189
00:15:30,888 --> 00:15:35,893
We shouldn't keep secrets

190
00:15:37,811 --> 00:15:39,146
from each other.

191
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:41,815
Okay?

192
00:15:41,899 --> 00:15:47,404
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

193
00:15:47,488 --> 00:15:48,656
<i>Boss.</i>

194
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:51,200
<i>Why don't you just tell her how you feel?</i>

195
00:15:54,328 --> 00:15:56,914
<i>Now's really not the time</i>
<i>to mess with her head.</i>

196
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:01,502
<i>I'm just waiting for the right time.</i>

197
00:16:05,297 --> 00:16:09,176
<i>I think, boss, for now,</i>

198
00:16:09,259 --> 00:16:12,763
<i>it's better if you just let her know that</i>
<i>you'll always be there for her.</i>

199
00:16:13,764 --> 00:16:14,974
<i>Okay.</i>

200
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:16,809
<i>Yeah?</i> [CHUCKLES]

201
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:21,146
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

202
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:23,440
<i>Um, I just wanted to ask something.</i>

203
00:16:24,274 --> 00:16:25,401
<i>What is it?</i>

204
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:27,444
<i>Are we okay?</i>

205
00:16:28,362 --> 00:16:30,072
<i>Yeah. What do you mean?</i>

206
00:16:30,823 --> 00:16:32,741
<i>There's something you're not telling me.</i>

207
00:16:36,078 --> 00:16:40,374
<i>Jordan, say it. Come on.</i>

208
00:16:40,457 --> 00:16:41,333
<i>What is it?</i>

209
00:16:41,417 --> 00:16:46,505
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

210
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:48,298
[TIRES SCREECHING]

211
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:49,508
[GRUNTS]

212
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:52,302
[DINO GRUNTS]

213
00:16:53,512 --> 00:16:54,471
- <i>Boss!</i>
- [DINO GROANS]

214
00:17:01,061 --> 00:17:02,104
<i>Dad?</i>

215
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:05,357
<i>Be careful, Jordan.</i>

216
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:07,359
<i>Watch out for Caloy.</i>

217
00:17:07,443 --> 00:17:14,450
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

218
00:17:15,075 --> 00:17:16,785
[MUSIC FADES]

219
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:20,706
[OLIVER] Billy?

220
00:17:21,373 --> 00:17:23,000
- Billy!
- Hello.

221
00:17:23,625 --> 00:17:25,544
- You don't have work?
- Mm-hmm.

222
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:30,883
Your sister's here because
we're going somewhere together.

223
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:32,009
Where?

224
00:17:33,469 --> 00:17:35,471
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

225
00:17:35,554 --> 00:17:36,889
You know, Oliver,

226
00:17:36,972 --> 00:17:40,768
sometimes, even grown-ups

227
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:43,937
still keep secrets.

228
00:17:45,397 --> 00:17:47,691
Because they're scared that

229
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:52,529
if their loved ones find out
about this secret,

230
00:17:53,697 --> 00:17:56,533
they'll get hurt or push them away.

231
00:17:56,617 --> 00:18:02,706
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

232
00:18:04,041 --> 00:18:07,377
Our dad's scared right now…

233
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:11,882
because he kept a secret from us.

234
00:18:14,134 --> 00:18:16,303
What's his secret?

235
00:18:19,223 --> 00:18:20,933
You know,

236
00:18:21,016 --> 00:18:23,268
I just found out recently that…

237
00:18:25,312 --> 00:18:27,940
we have other siblings.

238
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:30,609
What?

239
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:37,366
You know, I was also shocked
when I found out.

240
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:43,789
And I know you must have
so many questions.

241
00:18:46,583 --> 00:18:50,462
You can ask me or Auntie Pres, okay?

242
00:18:54,883 --> 00:18:56,218
You don't have to though.

243
00:18:57,719 --> 00:18:59,721
Whatever helps you deal with it.

244
00:19:00,848 --> 00:19:03,725
If they're our siblings,

245
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:06,311
why aren't they with us?

246
00:19:10,691 --> 00:19:16,071
They were raised in a different family.

247
00:19:17,322 --> 00:19:20,534
Their mother was the one who raised them.

248
00:19:21,326 --> 00:19:23,579
That's why we didn't meet them sooner.

249
00:19:24,997 --> 00:19:26,665
Where are they?

250
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:30,836
Your sister and your father
are waiting for you now.

251
00:19:30,919 --> 00:19:34,339
[PRECIOUS] I'll go with you
if you want to meet her.

252
00:19:38,302 --> 00:19:40,470
[BILLY] But no one's forcing you, okay?

253
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:43,724
It's okay if you're not ready
to meet her yet.

254
00:19:47,936 --> 00:19:51,148
What matters is you know the truth now.

255
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:56,737
Where are they?

256
00:19:57,487 --> 00:19:59,740
Where are we going to meet them?

257
00:19:59,823 --> 00:20:05,829
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

258
00:20:20,177 --> 00:20:21,511
[BEA] <i>Oh.</i>

259
00:20:21,595 --> 00:20:23,055
<i>Uh…</i>

260
00:20:23,138 --> 00:20:24,556
<i>I'm Bea.</i>

261
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:29,436
<i>I'm your sister too.</i>

262
00:20:31,521 --> 00:20:32,940
<i>If you want,</i>

263
00:20:33,023 --> 00:20:35,359
<i>you can call me</i>

264
00:20:36,026 --> 00:20:37,152
<i>Big Sister Bea.</i>

265
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:39,071
<i>I still can't believe</i>

266
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:41,907
<i>that we're together again.</i>

267
00:20:43,575 --> 00:20:44,534
<i>Me neither.</i>

268
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:47,996
<i>But it would be much better</i>
<i>if Mama were here too.</i>

269
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:50,249
<i>You know we can't</i>
<i>do that right now.</i>

270
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:52,793
<i>Ms. Tere, I've changed.</i>

271
00:20:52,876 --> 00:20:54,795
<i>I'll take on any job you give me.</i>

272
00:20:54,878 --> 00:20:56,046
<i>A job?</i>

273
00:20:56,129 --> 00:20:57,631
<i>You're an ex-convict.</i>

274
00:20:57,714 --> 00:21:00,801
<i>Who would trust you?</i>

275
00:21:00,884 --> 00:21:02,302
<i>No one.</i>

276
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:04,972
<i>You might even make me</i>
<i>lose customers.</i>

277
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:06,974
<i>- Leave you alone?</i>
<i>- Ouch!</i>

278
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:11,186
<i>Want me to call the cops on you, huh?</i>

279
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:12,187
<i>Hey, give those back!</i>

280
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:14,356
<i>- Those belong to my customer!</i>
<i>- Where's Caloy?</i>

281
00:21:15,857 --> 00:21:17,317
<i>Where's Caloy?!</i>

282
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:44,803
<i>Bea.</i>

283
00:21:45,804 --> 00:21:46,722
<i>Caloy.</i>

284
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:49,808
[BOTH LAUGHING SOFTLY]

285
00:21:49,891 --> 00:21:51,226
<i>I missed you.</i>

286
00:21:54,146 --> 00:21:55,397
<i>I love you.</i>

287
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:58,275
- <i>I missed you.</i>
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

288
00:21:58,775 --> 00:22:00,736
<i>W-What happened to you?</i>

289
00:22:00,819 --> 00:22:03,280
<i>I looked for you. I-It was-- Goodness.</i>

290
00:22:03,363 --> 00:22:04,656
<i>How did you get out?</i>

291
00:22:05,574 --> 00:22:06,575
<i>Uh…</i>

292
00:22:08,076 --> 00:22:09,161
<i>Because of Billy.</i>

293
00:22:09,786 --> 00:22:11,246
<i>Billy forgave me.</i>

294
00:22:13,790 --> 00:22:14,916
<i>Really?</i>

295
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:16,918
<i>How?</i>

296
00:22:17,753 --> 00:22:18,712
<i>And why?</i>
